1.AT LEAST K OCCURENCES 
Given an array arr. Return the element that occurs at least k number of times.
Note:
If there are multiple answers, please return the first one.
If there is no element found, return -1.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int firstElementKTime(int[] arr, int k) {
                HashMap<Integer,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
                for(int num:arr){
                    map.put(num,map.getOrDefault(num,0)+1);
                    if(map.get(num)==k){
                        return num;
                    }
                }
                return -1;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/first-element-to-occur-k-times5150/1


2.PAIRS WITH DIFFERENCE K 
Given an array arr[] of positive integers. Find the number of pairs of integers whose absolute difference equals to a given number k.
Note: (a, b) and (b, a) are considered the same. Also, the same numbers at different indices are considered different.
The answer is guaranteed to fit in a 32-bit integer.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            int countPairs(int[] arr, int k) {
                int count=0;
                HashMap<Integer,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
                for(int num:arr){
                    map.put(num,map.getOrDefault(num,0)+1);
                }
                if(k==0){
                    for(int freq:map.values()){
                        count+=freq*(freq-1)/2;
                    }
                } 
                else{
                    for(int num:map.keySet()){
                        if(map.containsKey(num+k)){
                            count+=map.get(num)*map.get(num+k);
                        }
                    }
                }
                return count;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/pairs-with-difference-k1713/1


3.GREATEST ON RIGHT SIDE 
You are given an array arr[]. Replace every element with the next greatest element (the greatest element on its right side) in the array. 
Note: There is no element next to the last element, so replace it with -1.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            static ArrayList<Integer> nextGreatest(int arr[]) {
                ArrayList<Integer> list=new ArrayList<>();
                int max=-1;
                for(int i=arr.length-1;i>=0;i--){
                    int temp=arr[i];
                    arr[i]=max;
                    max=Math.max(max,temp);
                }
                for(int num:arr) {
                    list.add(num);
                }
                return list;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/greater-on-right-side4305/1


4.K-TH MISSING IN SORTED 
Given an increasing sequence arr, we need to find the K-th smallest missing element, taking the first element of the array as the starting point in the increasing sequence. 
If there is no k-th missing element then output -1.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            int KthMissingElement(int arr[], int k) {
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length-1;i++){
                    int missing=arr[i+1]-arr[i]-1;
                    if (k<=missing) {
                        return arr[i]+k;
                    }
                    k-=missing;
                }
                return -1;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/k-th-missing-element3635/1
